  ],
  "text": "Stay awake seventeen hours and your reaction times match a legally drunk driver. You would never drive after four drinks. You will happily drive after a long day. Push it to twenty four hours and the impairment roughly doubles. Judgement goes first, then emotional control, then your immune response. But here is the dangerous part. Sleep loss removes your ability to notice sleep loss. People tested while sleep deprived rate their own performance as fine. It is not. Which is why almost nobody who says they function on five hours is measuring anything. A very small number of people genuinely do carry a gene variant for short sleep. It is rare enough that if you are wondering whether you have it, you do not. Most people who need less sleep have simply got used to performing worse. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
